  "description": "Shenora's Android shell: the MAUI HybridWebView IPC transport (the same envelope the desktop shell speaks, over SendRawMessage/RawMessageReceived), the resource interceptor that answers a page's byte ranges, a UI-thread dispatcher, safe-area insets, the SYSTEM BACK GESTURE offered to the page before the platform finishes the activity under it, foreground transitions carrying how long the app was away, holding the window portrait or landscape (which a page can only do in fullscreen), and the Android implementations of the Shenora shell contracts — native file dialogs, a MediaCodec-backed audio and video conversion pipeline with device capability probing, an ExoPlayer/MediaPlayer media player, and a MediaSession playback session for the lock screen and headphone controls. The platform owns the loop, so the app drives ShenoraApplication.Start/Stop from its own lifecycle rather than calling Run. Shares its source with Shenora.iOS.",
